    <string name="explain_a11y_body">Android offers this switch for apps that need to act on the whole phone. Calm Launcher uses it for two things only:\n\n• Lock the screen when you double tap the home screen.\n• See the name of the app that just opened, so your pauses, limits and focus mode also work when an app is opened from a notification, a link or another launcher.\n\nWhat it never does: read what is on the screen, read what you type, take screenshots, or send anything anywhere. The launcher has no internet access at all.\n\nTo turn it on: tap Continue, find Calm Launcher in the list (sometimes under \"Downloaded apps\" or \"Installed services\"), and switch it on. You can switch it off the same way at any time.</string>
    <string name="explain_a11y_title">Focus helper (accessibility)</string>
    <string name="explain_continue">Continue to settings</string>
    <string name="explain_manage">Open settings to change</string>
    <string name="explain_not_now">Not now</string>
    <string name="explain_notif_body">This lets Calm Launcher apply the notification rules you set: allow, silence, or collect in the digest.\n\nDigest items (title and text) are stored only in the launcher\'s private storage on this phone so you can read them later. They are never sent anywhere, and you can clear them at any time.\n\nCalls, alarms, navigation and ongoing notifications are always left alone.\n\nTap Continue, then switch on Calm Launcher.</string>
    <string name="explain_notif_title">Notification access</string>
    <string name="explain_overlay_body">Only needed if you use the fallback monitor instead of the focus helper. It lets the pause screen appear on top of an app you limited. Without it, you\'ll get a notification instead.\n\nTap Continue, then allow Calm Launcher.</string>
    <string name="explain_overlay_title">Display over other apps</string>
    <string name="explain_status_granted">Status: on</string>
    <string name="explain_status_not_granted">Status: off</string>
    <string name="explain_usage_body">Daily time limits and usage insights need to know how long you have used each app today. Android keeps this record on your phone. Usage access lets Calm Launcher read it.\n\nThe numbers are only read on this phone, only when needed, and never leave it.\n\nTap Continue, find Calm Launcher, and allow usage access.</string>
